  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow`. The requirement says the skill must open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps.\n\n- **First section:** After the `# Habeas` title and a short introductory preamble, the first `##` section is `## Workflow`. The preamble is lead-in text under the title, not a separate section. The other sections (`Testing and coverage artifacts`, `Inspecting`, `Requirements, examples, and definitions`, `References`, `Gotchas`) all come after it. The sibling skill `assets/skills/habeas-refactor/SKILL.md` has the same layout: a title, a brief intro, then `## Workflow`.\n- **Ordered steps:** The workflow is a numbered checklist, `- [ ] 1.` (pick the skill from a table) followed by `- [ ] 2.` (follow that skill and the move-then-edit rule). A short note about running commands from the project root follows the steps.\n- **Violation matches:** There were none to judge.\n\nI found no gap against this requirement.",
